#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""drover: send a task to the project it belongs to and start a coding agent there in herdr.

    drover "the gate camera stopped recording"     route, open a herdr tab, start the agent
    drover                                         read the task from stdin (paste, then Ctrl-D)
    drover -n "..."                                show where it would go and why; start nothing
    drover @infra "..."   drover -C ~/x "..."      skip routing
    drover places                                  list the places and what the model is told
    drover eval [--model] [--limit N] [--wrong]    replay your Claude Code history through the router

Rules decide first and a local model is asked only when they cannot:
  explicit   @place at the start of the task, or -C DIR
  path       a path in the task that lies inside a place, or a relative path that exists in one
  name       a place named in the task
  keyword    the [keywords] of the config
  history    the places where your most similar past Claude Code sessions ran
  model      an OpenAI-compatible model, given every place's one-line description
  default    the configured default place

Python 3.9+ standard library only. Configuration: ~/.config/drover/config.ini (see config.example.ini).
"""

